    "DIAGNOSIS": {
      "present": true,
      "status": "content",
      "content_blocks": [
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "level": 0,
          "text": "Generally presumptive, based on acute onset of signs in a patient with predisposing factors, Transmural infarction of the left ventricle in a dog with arteriosclerosis and hypothyroidism. The first three rapid successive complexes represent ventricular tachycardia. The sinus rhythm that follows illustrates small complexes, marked elevation of the ST segment, and first‐degree atrioventricular block (prolonged PR interval). (Source: From Tilley LP. Essentials of Canine and Feline Electrocardiography, 3rd ed. Baltimore: Williams & Wilkins, 1992. Reprinted with permission of Wolters Kluwer.)",
          "pdf_page": 1015,
          "printed_page": 933,
          "column": 1
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "level": 0,
          "text": "consistent ECG changes (ST segment changes) and elevated circulating biomarkers (cardiac troponin I [cTnI]).",
          "pdf_page": 1015,
          "printed_page": 933,
          "column": 2
        }
      ],
